-- title:
--   Chartwise p-th power endomorphism acts on places by q-expansion Frobenius
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a positive integer $M$ with $p \mid M$, a subgroup $H$ of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, and assume the $q$-expansion $j$-series `jqModC ℚ` lies in the $q$-expansion function field $F_\mathbb{Q}$ of level $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$ (the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}$-Laurent series generated by ratios of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of equal weight). Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, whose residue field $\kappa$ is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$, and let $\rho : \mathtt{R}\,p \to A$ be a ring homomorphism whose composite with the inclusion $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is the structural map; $\kappa$ is an `R p`-algebra via $\rho$ followed by the residue map. Let $\Gamma' = \mathtt{ΓN}\,p\,M\,H\,hpM$ and let $\mathrm{Mfib}$ be a curve model of the $q$-expansion function field $F_\kappa$ of level $\Gamma'$ over $\kappa$: an integral scheme, proper and smooth of relative dimension $1$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\kappa$, with a ring isomorphism `ffEquiv` onto its function field over the base and a bijection `placeOfPoint` from closed points to places of $F_\kappa$ over $\kappa$ whose valuation subring is the image of the stalk. Assume $e_{\mathrm{fib}} : \mathrm{Mfib}.C \to \mathfrak{X}_\kappa$ is an isomorphism onto the fibre over $\operatorname{Spec}\kappa$ of the two-chart integral model `toBase p Γ' hj`, compatible with the base morphisms, with nonempty preimage of the image of the $j$-finite chart, and satisfying the dictionary `Mfib_pin`: for $b$ in the finite chart algebra `chartAlgFin p Γ' hj` and $y$ a Laurent series over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is the $q$-expansion of $b$, the function-field element obtained by pulling $b$ back along $e_{\mathrm{fib}}$ followed by the first projection and taking its germ at the generic point has Laurent series the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal. Assume further that $F_\kappa$ is finite as a module over itself along the $q$-expansion Frobenius $\Phi : f(q) \mapsto f(q^p)$, and let $\theta$ be an endomorphism of $\mathfrak{X}_\kappa$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\kappa$. Then for every morphism $c_0$ from $\operatorname{Spec}(\kappa \otimes_{\mathtt{R}p} \mathtt{chartAlgFin}\,p\,\Gamma'\,hj)$ to $\mathfrak{X}_\kappa$ whose composites with the two projections are given by $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the right inclusion followed by the $j$-finite chart immersion `ιFin` and by $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the left inclusion respectively, every $\kappa$-algebra endomorphism $\varphi$ of $\kappa \otimes_{\mathtt{R}p} \mathtt{chartAlgFin}$ with $\varphi(1 \otimes b) = (1 \otimes b)^p$ for all chart functions $b$ and with $c_0$ followed by $\theta$ equal to $\operatorname{Spec}\varphi$ followed by $c_0$, and every closed point $P$ of $\mathrm{Mfib}.C$: the point $e_{\mathrm{fib}}^{-1}(\theta(e_{\mathrm{fib}}(P)))$ is again a closed point, and its associated place equals the place obtained from that of $P$ by restriction along $\Phi$, i.e. `qExpFrobeniusPlaceModL` applied to $\mathrm{Mfib}.placeOfPoint\,P$.
--
--   This is the Deligne–Rapoport dictionary reading of the Frobenius action in characteristic $p$: an endomorphism of the $\kappa$-fibre of the two-chart integral model which is the $p$-th power map on the $j$-finite chart induces, on closed points transported through the curve model, the Frobenius twist of places of the $q$-expansion function field. It supplies the place clauses used in the construction of the Deligne–Rapoport model data at $p$, and is cited by [`ModularCurve.XHDRLevel.comp1_pi_place_and_pi_w_comp0_place_of_chart_atkinLehner`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRLevel.comp1_pi_place_and_pi_w_comp0_place_of_chart_atkinLehner) and [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_placeOfPoint_frobeniusTwist_eq_smul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_placeOfPoint_frobeniusTwist_eq_smul).
